WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.781
Sara Says No! by Norman Whitney.

00:00:18.841 --> 00:00:23.413
Welcome to Middletown!

00:00:23.473 --> 00:00:26.134
It is Monday morning.

00:00:26.194 --> 00:00:29.456
Everybody is at the market.

00:00:29.516 --> 00:00:32.196
The market is busy.

00:00:32.257 --> 00:00:36.968
Today, there is a new man at the market.

00:00:37.028 --> 00:00:40.318
His name is Mister Fruit.

00:00:40.378 --> 00:00:43.898
His daughter is helping him.

00:00:43.958 --> 00:00:47.050
Her name is Sara.

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:49.232
Good morning,

00:00:49.292 --> 00:00:52.185
Mister Fruit says to everybody.

00:00:52.245 --> 00:00:54.377
My fruit is fresh.

00:00:54.437 --> 00:00:56.799
My fruit is cheap.

00:00:56.858 --> 00:00:59.662
Mister Fruit is polite.

00:00:59.722 --> 00:01:02.123
He is friendly.

00:01:02.183 --> 00:01:05.876
Everybody likes Mister Fruit.

00:01:05.936 --> 00:01:10.500
What a nice man! they say. 

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.309
Everybody likes his daughter.

00:01:14.369 --> 00:01:19.400
What a nice girl! they say.
  
00:01:19.552 --> 00:01:25.217
A schoolboy asks for one kilo of apples.

00:01:25.276 --> 00:01:30.220
Mister Fruit puts some apples on the scales.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:36.534
The scales show one kilo and one hundred grammes.

00:01:36.594 --> 00:01:41.018
Mister Fruit takes one apple away.

00:01:41.078 --> 00:01:46.234
Now the scales show nine hundred grammes.

00:01:46.294 --> 00:01:49.196
But Mister Fruit says,

00:01:49.256 --> 00:01:52.969
One kilo of apples! One dollar!

00:01:53.029 --> 00:01:56.972
He takes one dollar from the schoolboy.

00:01:57.032 --> 00:02:00.484
Sara is watching her father.

00:02:00.544 --> 00:02:04.477
She sees everything.

00:02:04.537 --> 00:02:11.111
A young woman asks for two kilos of oranges.

00:02:11.171 --> 00:02:16.424
Mister Fruit puts some oranges on the scales.

00:02:16.484 --> 00:02:22.388
The scales show two kilos and two hundred grammes.

00:02:22.448 --> 00:02:26.811
Mister Fruit takes one orange away.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:33.504
Now the scales show one kilo and eight hundred grammes.

00:02:33.564 --> 00:02:36.606
But Mister Fruit says,

00:02:36.666 --> 00:02:40.774
Two kilos of oranges! Two dollars!

00:02:40.834 --> 00:02:45.172
He takes two dollars from the young woman.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:50.456
Sara sees everything.

00:02:50.516 --> 00:02:54.960
It is Monday evening.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:59.400
Sara’s father is counting his money.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:01.266
He is happy.

00:03:01.326 --> 00:03:04.198
But Sara is not happy.

00:03:04.258 --> 00:03:09.213
She is angry.

00:03:09.273 --> 00:03:16.820
Father! You must sell the correct weight!

00:03:16.879 --> 00:03:19.772
You mustn’t cheat our customers.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:22.243
Our customers are poor.

00:03:22.303 --> 00:03:25.245
But we are poor too, Sara!

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:27.156
My wife is dead.

00:03:27.216 --> 00:03:29.268
You have no mother.

00:03:29.328 --> 00:03:31.620
I have no sons.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.891
You have no brothers.

00:03:33.951 --> 00:03:36.372
We must make money, Sara!

00:03:36.432 --> 00:03:38.014
That’s life!

00:03:38.074 --> 00:03:41.756
I don’t want to work at the market, Father.

00:03:41.816 --> 00:03:44.237
You must work at the market!

00:03:44.297 --> 00:03:46.278
We must live, Sara.

00:03:46.338 --> 00:03:47.998
We must eat!

00:03:48.058 --> 00:03:50.239
You’re a child.

00:03:50.299 --> 00:03:53.040
You don’t understand business.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:54.881
You’re a woman.

00:03:54.941 --> 00:03:57.962
Women don’t understand business.

00:03:58.022 --> 00:04:03.664
That’s life, Sara!

00:04:03.724 --> 00:04:09.716
It is Tuesday morning.

00:04:09.776 --> 00:04:14.968
Today, Sara’s father is selling the correct weight.

00:04:15.028 --> 00:04:17.031
He is honest.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.822
He takes the correct money.

00:04:19.882 --> 00:04:22.334
Sara is happy.

00:04:22.394 --> 00:04:26.278
Today, she is proud of her father.

00:04:26.338 --> 00:04:30.010
The customers are happy too.

00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:33.302
They buy a lot of fruit.

00:04:33.362 --> 00:04:38.950
Your fruit is cheap and fresh, they say. 

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:44.905
But in the afternoon, some customers come back.

00:04:44.964 --> 00:04:47.226
They are angry.

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:51.527
An old man brings back some apples.

00:04:51.587 --> 00:04:55.008
One of his apples is bad.

00:04:55.068 --> 00:04:58.900
A girl brings back some oranges.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:02.300
One of her oranges is bad.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:06.152
A woman brings back some bananas.

00:05:06.212 --> 00:05:09.464
One of her bananas is bad.

00:05:09.524 --> 00:05:13.786
It is black and full of worms.

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:16.547
Look, Mister Fruit!

00:05:16.607 --> 00:05:19.978
Your fruit isn’t fresh today.

00:05:20.038 --> 00:05:23.620
We want our money back!

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:27.731
But Mister Fruit does not listen.

00:05:27.791 --> 00:05:32.922
He does not give them any money.

00:05:32.982 --> 00:05:39.200
You’re dishonest, Father! says Sara.
 
00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:41.865
You’re cheating the customers!

00:05:41.925 --> 00:05:44.556
I don’t want to work for you.

00:05:44.616 --> 00:05:47.568
I don’t want to work at the market!

00:05:47.628 --> 00:05:50.610
But you must work for me, Sara,

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:52.260
says her father.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:54.200
I have no family!

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:57.373
I have no wife and no sons.

00:05:57.433 --> 00:06:00.314
Children must help their parents.

00:06:00.374 --> 00:06:04.236
You are my daughter, Sara. You must work for me.
 
00:06:04.296 --> 00:06:05.687
That’s life!

00:06:05.747 --> 00:06:08.800
No, Father, says Sara.
 
00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:11.834
I don’t want to clean your house.
 
00:06:11.893 --> 00:06:13.985
I want to leave home.

00:06:14.045 --> 00:06:17.038
I don’t want to cook your food.

00:06:17.097 --> 00:06:19.860
I want to get a good job!

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:23.182
I’m not going to work for you.

00:06:23.242 --> 00:06:26.215
Sara’s father is angry.

00:06:26.274 --> 00:06:30.898
Go to bed! he shouts at her.
 
00:06:30.958 --> 00:06:34.180
Sara goes to bed.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.210
She is lonely.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:38.379
She is unhappy.

00:06:38.439 --> 00:06:40.790
She says a prayer.

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:46.123
Please help me. Please help my father.
 
00:06:46.183 --> 00:06:50.015
Please help us.

00:06:50.075 --> 00:06:53.597
What am I going to do?

00:06:53.657 --> 00:06:56.689
I need a miracle.

00:06:56.748 --> 00:06:59.109
Help me!

00:06:59.229 --> 00:07:05.328
It is Wednesday morning.

00:07:05.388 --> 00:07:08.364
Everybody is at the market.

00:07:08.424 --> 00:07:11.275
Everybody is laughing.

00:07:11.335 --> 00:07:14.996
Something strange is happening.

00:07:15.056 --> 00:07:18.968
Mister Fruit touches an apple.

00:07:19.028 --> 00:07:22.290
The apple goes bad.

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:25.451
Then he picks up an orange.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:28.662
The orange goes bad too.

00:07:28.722 --> 00:07:32.343
Then he picks up some bananas.

00:07:32.403 --> 00:07:35.157
They go black.

00:07:35.217 --> 00:07:44.306
Everybody laughs. Look at Mister Fruit!
 
00:07:44.366 --> 00:07:49.430
He touches the fruit and it goes bad!

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:53.984
Mister Fruit looks at his hands.

00:07:54.044 --> 00:08:01.680
What is happening? he says. Please, Sara. Please help me.
 
00:08:01.739 --> 00:08:05.036
Sara touches an apple.

00:08:05.096 --> 00:08:09.432
She picks up an orange and some bananas.

00:08:09.492 --> 00:08:16.904
Hooray! everybody says. It’s a miracle!
 
00:08:16.964 --> 00:08:22.126
Sara touches the fruit and it’s OK!

00:08:22.186 --> 00:08:29.979
We’re going to buy our fruit from Sara!

00:08:30.038 --> 00:08:38.756
Next year, Mister Fruit is Miss Fruit.

00:08:38.815 --> 00:08:41.648
Sara is honest.

00:08:41.708 --> 00:08:43.990
She does not cheat.

00:08:44.049 --> 00:08:47.572
She always sells the correct weight.

00:08:47.632 --> 00:08:51.036
She sells good, fresh fruit.

00:08:51.096 --> 00:08:54.339
She understands business.

00:08:54.399 --> 00:08:58.051
Sara is making a lot of money.

00:08:58.112 --> 00:09:01.788
She has a good job now.

00:09:01.848 --> 00:09:05.955
Sara’s father stays at home.

00:09:06.015 --> 00:09:08.446
He cleans the house.

00:09:08.506 --> 00:09:10.588
He cooks the food.

00:09:10.648 --> 00:09:12.900
He is very happy.

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:31.000
That’s life! he says.
 
